  "term": "mass-spring model",
  "definition": "A mass-spring model is a network model in which nodes act like masses connected by springs, allowing researchers to examine how the arrangement of masses across the network changes the system’s vibration frequencies. In this source, it is used to study how matching mass placement to node position influences overall collective dynamics.",
